# Explore — routed read-only search

A broad sweep over the repo that reads excerpts to locate things. It does not review, audit or
judge code, and it writes nothing.

**Why this file exists.** The tier mapping (`references/model-optimization.md`,
*Mapping + ceiling*) sends read-only work with no Options to the **light** tier. Carrying that
pair here makes the route **declarative**: it attaches to the agent type instead of depending on
whatever spawns it, so an orchestrator, a worker, and an agent three levels down all get the same
route with nothing to remember.

**Precedence, so the override still works.** A per-invocation `model` or `effort` argument beats
this frontmatter, and `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` beats it too. That is the intended shape: this
file is the **floor** for the type, and an explicit route on a particular dispatch is the
override. A sweep that genuinely needs more than the floor says so at the call site.

**Change the pair only with the mapping.** If this repo's tier mapping moves, move this file with
it; a definition that disagrees with the mapping is a second, drifting copy of the routing policy.
